,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
1,Tulishi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulishi_language,"Tulishi (Kuntulishi, Thulishi, Tulesh) is a Kadu language spoken in South Kordofan. Dialects are Tulishi proper and Kamdang. Ethnologue (22nd edition) lists dialects as: The Dar el Kabira and Kamdang dialects are reportedly similar.",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
2,Tulishi language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/tulishi_language,"The Tulishi language, a member of the Kadu branch of the Nilo-Saharan family (though previously classified under Niger-Congo), features three primary dialects: Tulishi proper, Kamda (also known as Kamdang), and Dar El Kabira.",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
3,Tulishi people — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/tulishi_people,"The Tulishi people, known to themselves as the Gatulishi, are a small indigenous ethnic group residing in the Nuba Mountains of South Kordofan state, Sudan. [1]",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
4,Tulishi - tey (Nilo-Saharan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://www.peoplegroups.org/language/tey/,"Language Profile Tulishi (tey) Tulishi (tey) is part of the Nilo-Saharan family and Nilo-Saharan, Satellite-Core, Core, Kadugli-Krongo class.",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
5,Tiwizi | Tuareg Blues Guitar • Sahara Desert Music & North ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yjboW3ayB7U,"Aug 30, 2025 · This track blends Tuareg blues guitar, Sahara desert music, and North African fusion instrumental vibes into a soulful journey across the dunes.",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
6,Tulishi | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/tey/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..h73HbdyDSp_IaHeVz5OrOrWeJu18xF8Pn13RgDK1HE4,Tulishi is an endangered indigenous language of Sudan. It belongs to the Nilo-Saharan language family.,Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
7,Tulishi - tey (Nilo-Saharan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/tey/,"Tulishi (tey) is part of the Nilo-Saharan family and Nilo-Saharan, Satellite-Core, Core, Kadugli-Krongo class.",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
8,Tulishi,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Tulishi,"Language family: Nilo-Saharan, Kadugli-Krongo (SIL classification). Number of speakers: ~2,500. Vulnerability: Threatened. Script: Latin script. More information: Tulishi is spoken in Sudan, Africa.",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
9,Nilo-Saharan Languages - SourceWatch,https://www.sourcewatch.org/index.php/Nilo-Saharan_Languages,"Nilo-Saharan Languages are a family of 205 languages. The most common are Dholuo in Kenya and Kanuri in Nigeria with 3.5 million speakers each.Kadugli-Krongo: Kanga, Katcha-Kadugli-Miri, Keiga, Krongo, Tulishi, and Tumtum (all spoken in Sudan).",Tulishi,Nilo-Saharan
